course: dictionary
lesson: 13028
title: Faddy and the clues around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how a person behaves, and the words around them tell you what the behaviour is. «Ben is a faddy eater, so he will only eat pasta and bread.» Ben refuses most foods, so faddy must mean fussy about food.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence: «Our cat is very faddy about her food and sniffs every bowl before she takes one bite.» Sniffing and refusing both show she is picky. Swap in the word picky and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Faddy can also mean following fashions that do not last long. «Last year everyone wore glow-in-the-dark trainers, but it was a faddy craze and soon nobody cared.» The words soon nobody cared show that the fashion was short-lived.
fact: Faddy is an adjective, so it can change: faddy, faddier, faddiest.
fact: «Faddy» means fussy about food, liking only a few things and refusing many others.
fact: «Faddy» can also mean following short-lived fashions or crazes.
fact: A faddy eater is a picky eater, and people often say «faddy about food».
fact: Faddy is mostly used in British English, especially by parents and grandparents.
exercise: «Ben is a faddy eater, so he will only eat pasta and bread.» What does faddy mean here? | *Fussy about food, liking only a few things | Very tall | Fond of running races | Hungry all day
exercise: «Last year everyone wore glow-in-the-dark trainers, but it was a faddy craze.» What does faddy suggest about the craze? | It lasted for a hundred years | *It was popular for a short time | It was made of wood | It was a famous museum
exercise: Find and copy the word that means picky about food. «Our Lily is so faddy she won't touch a carrot.» | touch | Lily | carrot | *faddy
test: Mum says, «Dad is faddy, he eats the same cereal every single day.» What is the best meaning of faddy? | *Fussy and picky | Happy and loud | Very kind | Fast at running
test: A teacher says a fashion is faddy. What does she mean? | *It is popular now but will soon go out of style | It has been loved for centuries | It is the same as an old story | It is always the best choice
exam: Which sentence uses faddy correctly? | The faddy river runs down to the sea | *Ben is so faddy that he refuses peas, beans and fish | Yesterday the faddy train arrived at noon | I am a faddy eater who tries every food on the menu
